{"title":"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Ptolemy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Ptolemy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Elementary)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Elementary)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Coordinate_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Coordinate Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles right triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98c9384a46771f70b74fc9f54863602b4e6ac7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC=3$\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d83aebbbb8c767594aaccb3031d25a59585eac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI&gt;AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f130b65813b7c1ea07539ddf68a6b4dd390cd7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIME$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral. Given that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b41dff72d68d841b1af1ca99588855cc80aabc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EMI$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d37413bae1973358eebff164711f292d16be56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd09068a928d4670c9624f2e584be3e42e9498c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a-\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd64cd37b8cef5cc7154ed261604e3d7acb7e60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }9 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }10 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }11 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }12 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }13 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278b2e6e7fa77d2e7efc4741b2c1c194f758fc1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad;  size(200);  pair A, B, C, I, M, E;  A = (0, 0); B = (3, 0); C = (0, 3); M = (1.5, 1.5); I = (0, 1.5 + sqrt(2) / 2); E = (1.5 - sqrt(2) / 2, 0);  draw(A -- B -- C -- cycle); draw(I -- M -- E -- cycle); draw(rightanglemark(I, A, E, 4));  dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(I); dot(M); dot(E);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$I$&quot;, I, NE); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E + (0.1, 0.04), NE); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (A + C) / 2, W); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (A + B) / 2, S); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81602723dfaf6553b9d9f24d6c1cf36aad9069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EMI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles right (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of diameter arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f506b80246907627b4826e4d0fddd0a15f5913c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/8287f350ba7b9917b6196b074f52e9c425c2405c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle MEI = m\\angle MAI = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"216\" height=\"13\" />), so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/7045dc028a1b6028ff3335b8619adecfa8bf96c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MI=2,MC=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"155\" height=\"42\" />. With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0ba99839bf89bdea9afde607db21889b6edf38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{MCI}=45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, we can use Law of Cosines to determine that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2720c5004c3fff6f81744f8a5d11c478daaf192e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"41\" />. The same calculations hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> also, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc1a532eb6bebb69e112bcf7ee27ae2f4922320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI&lt;BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, we deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d37413bae1973358eebff164711f292d16be56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> is the smaller root, giving the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb61e766b085f513006f437a2dd96081fe314d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Ptolemy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Ptolemy)\">Solution 2 (Ptolemy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Ptolemy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81602723dfaf6553b9d9f24d6c1cf36aad9069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EMI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles and right.\n</p><p>Proof: Construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00d956df2ebf0b427a9bbb38a50624a0a1eadda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MF}\\perp\\overline{AB}$\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/9255608e91bc54be91202a3049df880957e36d62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MG}\\perp\\overline{AC}$\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41ee10c07baa91f100ec2eeca6b7b6ed3ab86698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2c830e136e667485791216de260e10db2c2195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, one can deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98c156af2cc0be7d33f56866331bf344fb741333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF=MG$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" />. Then by AAS it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57db8f80e63540e4b7fb328d11e643b465d8796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MI=ME$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81602723dfaf6553b9d9f24d6c1cf36aad9069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EMI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles. Since quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f130b65813b7c1ea07539ddf68a6b4dd390cd7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIME$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic, one can deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa8b057ed8f28cae6f2e52d5239126d75e98994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EMI}=90^\\circ$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. Q.E.D.\n</p><p>Since the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81602723dfaf6553b9d9f24d6c1cf36aad9069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EMI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is 2, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d0249c85abb0c4ba4bf6eacad400be2e16a290e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MI=ME=2$\" width=\"120\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dc794b346db74379d451c45066bfb54448cd604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI=2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the mid-point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffba394a1d83b19359057087c85fb8f373713ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b446805bf18c962118a8dd397d4bebce6030f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd7fddd8a1883d4d2c4517d0b7a832857200929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI=b$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />. By Ptolemy's Theorem, in cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f130b65813b7c1ea07539ddf68a6b4dd390cd7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIME$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed92fc152be843fa54fbd834bae6c7af904bee92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+2b=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. By Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574be94f7e262eac4697232ac7e21772adcafab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />. One can solve the simultaneous system and find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f292a627cd4f97dd0e919118b8812956e28160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{3+\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"41\" />. Then by deducting the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/35859a5c8d35dfe01d9946af6d086761edcfba63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AI}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> from 3 we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/3669ba7d635e628195b59d5faf0c81b9e5716415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"41\" />, giving the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb61e766b085f513006f437a2dd96081fe314d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />. (Surefire2019)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Elementary.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Elementary)\">Solution 3 (Elementary)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Elementary)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like above, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81602723dfaf6553b9d9f24d6c1cf36aad9069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EMI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles and right, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e3665f6ca1caa0dc7b8db75b31b1b0ddecd5aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{ME \\cdot MI}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c453cb3a53e61d7264d6bc83a650687bccf7ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MI^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707d00143277c5536b48ded84aa87ad7fb343b6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MI = 2$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. Then construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00d956df2ebf0b427a9bbb38a50624a0a1eadda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MF}\\perp\\overline{AB}$\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/9255608e91bc54be91202a3049df880957e36d62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MG}\\perp\\overline{AC}$\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> as well as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb953239e8f2213e04f7c546bca445229fde7f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MI}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. It's clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43db5665a7dbb6d1a5ae0a47f1067c942537beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MG^2+GI^2 = MI^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" /> by Pythagorean, so knowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793ff5760b93d428e7002cad5ca6e2020d3342c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MG = \\dfrac{AB}{2} = \\dfrac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" /> allows one to solve to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da7c366078a78873b8bc4d73c56a5da46a5bfd11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GI = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"41\" />. By just looking at the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cfbf342ddc3420cce9d73d90bef7a20442bb735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=AC-MF-GI=\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"260\" height=\"41\" />. The answer is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0d3f35d7d996f59d4a51eee8210c2071e60f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+7+2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Coordinate_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Coordinate_Geometry)\">Solution 4 (Coordinate Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Coordinate Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a40d2badbac4bdd4c5ffb5628c2e13a071bd14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f8c3a4b9b4588cd354272c3760b08ca53f16a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45aeeb9290e2989ecad6c63cbd75c1ed6dd66498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131e7249882acda72ddd7c1c316239c1ce1fcf71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${AIME}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b36805dea0a5a02d7fc16ff34be11dc6695277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EMI$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> (which is opposite of another right angle) must be a right angle; therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039f0fa1dac110aa35eacc0b1cf3ec486a2e72d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{ME} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{MI} = \\left&lt;\\frac{-3}{2}, y-\\frac{3}{2}\\right&gt; \\cdot \\left&lt;x-\\frac{3}{2}, -\\frac{3}{2}\\right&gt; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"363\" height=\"45\" />. Compute the dot product to arrive at the relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb87f9174dc56b66f9508cf580356e4eb8dd33ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. We can set up another equation involving the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dda2de59802a686642da56c34b5c729a9a22086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EMI$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a>. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debefff140e2770576456612afde3c94059ae30a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{3}{2}\\left(y-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-xy+\\frac{3}{2}\\left(x+\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\right].\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" /> Multiplying, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/5/3058f436e4c0042bcaf21e10b75d2d0f39eb0375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-x$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de4d306bef9a18c259c9285c1912282aee2cb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 -3x + \\frac{1}{2}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f09745a3271ac2271f5dcf741153ce9476c317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{7}}{2},\\frac{3 \\mp \\sqrt{7}}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"224\" height=\"55\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d83aebbbb8c767594aaccb3031d25a59585eac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI&gt;AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45b898c4fc1516b93a23f0aa401e51c36ccdbd10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=AI=\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096c904fc7d13e4fea9e14efb11f1f5d5d625e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI = 3-\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{7}}{2}=\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"224\" height=\"43\" />, and the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0d3f35d7d996f59d4a51eee8210c2071e60f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+7+2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Quick)\">Solution 5 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f130b65813b7c1ea07539ddf68a6b4dd390cd7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIME$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> cyclic we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a89cd2f387d2ebb73b78fa46de3adfb46efc09a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{MEI} = \\angle{MAI} = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b66c71ad6d8c6626574b4d532a19b6c240a5d647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{MIE} = \\angle{MAE} = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"189\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81602723dfaf6553b9d9f24d6c1cf36aad9069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EMI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles right triangle. \n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/3633ff8508b44c26db1242587d680d9ba70a9541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[EMI]=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f65088ffa51379a307466571f4d431f90f2f488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EM=MI=2$\" width=\"120\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386a3c1e645c9b09265419683a300307e07e2940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AEM} \\cong \\triangle{CIM}$\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/660bc1045d200200024acf7e6748a0da708bc586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AEM}=180-\\angle{AIM}=\\angle{CIM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"269\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62bd655cbf733a2ca9d1c660a108b55a9f457d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EM=IM$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b050f28428c151e875db7d55a05ecd15b3037b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAM}=\\angle{ICM}=45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"189\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e31ca5610717c87357c66f641a21e0b3200aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=AE=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5f5a5991ce066ac5084745d53e7f25074be1ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI=3-x$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>By Pythagoras on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21e56bd6f76785d6ff005d47363c8dc8f1b35d41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EAI}$\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/44263cb15416f98da2b1d92fc8e06bc762316cd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+(3-x)^2=EI^2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" />, and solve this to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8121451cc646f3d303a947349038dd756f85fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=CI=\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"140\" height=\"41\" /> for a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0d3f35d7d996f59d4a51eee8210c2071e60f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+7+2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Bash)\">Solution 6 (Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e7b3d2de1231eb7aa1592e1818b06e7652e3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=a$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee84ecdd61f515227fd7cf8ab785f56b04cb2e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=b$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Because opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0f9558ead3cef3db7a139f5cf4543ad718dec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EMI=90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. By the law of cosines, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb0fbae1f21d20ca805f89695b21b3da34111ca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MI^2=a^2+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b864e9704baf5d9c9f3ba3f2c4b62d6b550617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME^2=b^2+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600b7566e9bbc9fb166005a085bc256cda606e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI=2MO$\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the origin of the circle mentioned in the problem. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f23dbe04363b15623d93c616d9798288953df04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2MO*MO}{2}=2\\implies MO=\\sqrt{2}, EI=2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"353\" height=\"37\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/4589c5611339a397b1d1c1c34e3fb1a11fc3f425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME^2+MI^2=EI^2\\implies a^2+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}a+b^2+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}b=(2\\sqrt{2})^2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"530\" height=\"38\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/1733e2c72236b259156abbd2ddeec65286f31448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE^2+AI^2=EI^2\\implies (3-a)^2+(3-b)^2=(2\\sqrt{2})^2=8\\implies 18-6a-6b+a^2+b^2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"708\" height=\"21\" />. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9127ee2263d2a3ce52b4ad15b7157ae79f8d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18-6a-6b+a^2+b^2=a^2+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}a+b^2+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}b\\implies 18-6a-6b=\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}a-\\frac{3}{2}b\\implies \\frac{27}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"755\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10df21489d11ef3eac68dccfd1dfeaa4e24f0f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{9}{2}a+\\frac{9}{2}b\\implies a+b=3\\implies 3-b=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"332\" height=\"38\" />. We know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b36430d8e217a5b949e4d84775bf832f819b2c23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (3-a)^2+(3-b)^2&amp;=8 \\\\ (3-a)^2+a^2&amp;=8 \\\\ 2a^2-6a+9&amp;=8 \\\\ 2a^2-6a+1&amp;=0 \\\\ a&amp;=\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{36-8}}{2}=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{7}}{2}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"355\" height=\"152\" />\nWe take the smaller solution because we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652f31725c8f340ef02514d703f8cdbf6e17327b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI&gt;AE\\implies 3-AI&lt;3-AE\\implies CI&lt;CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"388\" height=\"13\" />, and we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d37413bae1973358eebff164711f292d16be56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />, not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/3669ba7d635e628195b59d5faf0c81b9e5716415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"41\" />. Thus our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0d3f35d7d996f59d4a51eee8210c2071e60f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+7+2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-vsamc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=4465\">https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=4465</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A\">2018 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem